VMA -- Virtual Memory Areas
===========================

Per-process record of *what* memory ranges are mapped. The page
table records *what is currently resident*; the VMA list records
*what should be there*. The two diverge under demand paging — a
VMA exists for a range, but the PTE is non-present until first
access. The page-fault handler consults the VMA list to decide
whether to install a fresh frame, copy-on-write, page-in from a
file, or kill the process.

Master-roadmap invariant 1: per-process VMA list, not fixed
regions. This module is the foundation chunk 1 lays before Phase
1's demand-paging / fork / exec work hits.

VMAs in a process never overlap. They form a sorted, disjoint
cover of the user portion of the address space. Lookups are by
address (point query): "which VMA covers `vaddr`?". This is
served by a red-black tree keyed on `start`, which gives O(log
n) insert, remove, and predecessor walk. (Augmented interval
trees aren't needed since VMAs don't overlap — the predecessor
of `vaddr` is the only candidate to check `vaddr < end` against.)

The pool is process-shared (one global free list). Each process
holds a `VMATree` root index. `vma_*` operations take the tree
by `*VMATree` and the global pool is module state.

This chunk is data-structure-only. No kernel codepath consults
the VMA list yet — the existing fixed-region eager-mapping in
`vm_create_process_pt` is unchanged. Chunk 2 wires the page-
fault handler through `vma_lookup_addr`; chunk 3 makes
`vm_create_process_pt` lazy.

    module oskit.kernel

    import oskit.config.{MAX_VMAS, PAGE_SIZE}
    import oskit.arch.{vm_install_user_page, vm_v2p}

VMA_NIL serves the same role as rbtree.lsysl's NIL — a sentinel
"no node" value distinct from any pool index.

    val VMA_NIL = -1

POSIX-style protection bits, used as the `prot` field of a VMA.
These match the values userspace uses for `mmap`/`mprotect`.

    val VMA_PROT_NONE  = 0
    val VMA_PROT_READ  = 1
    val VMA_PROT_WRITE = 2
    val VMA_PROT_EXEC  = 4

POSIX-style mapping bits, used as the low half of `flags`. The
high half is reserved for VMA-internal flags (COW, growsdown,
etc.) so an `mmap`-style argument can be stored without conflict.

    val VMA_MAP_SHARED  = 0x01
    val VMA_MAP_PRIVATE = 0x02
    val VMA_MAP_FIXED   = 0x10
    val VMA_MAP_ANON    = 0x20

Internal bits — set by the kernel, never accepted from userspace.

    val VMA_FLAG_COW       = 0x10000
    val VMA_FLAG_GROWSDOWN = 0x20000

Red-black colors. RED on insert, BLACK after fixup balances. The
root is always BLACK.

    val VMA_RB_BLACK = 0
    val VMA_RB_RED   = 1

A VMA carries the user-visible mapping fields (start/end/prot/
flags/fd/offset) plus its rb-tree-node fields (left/right/parent/
color) and a free-list link. Inlining the tree node into the VMA
struct avoids a parallel array — the same pool index serves both
the data and the tree node.

    struct VMA
        vstart: u64
        vend:   u64
        prot:   int
        flags:  int
        fd:     int
        offset: u64
        left:   int
        right:  int
        parent: int
        color:  int
        next_free: int

A `VMATree` is just the root index. Each process owns one. The
struct exists (instead of a bare `int` field) so operations can
take `*VMATree` and update `root` via field assignment, which
matches the rbtree.lsysl convention.

    struct VMATree
        root: int

Module-level pool. `MAX_VMAS` is set in `sysl.toml`/`oskit.config`
so the limit is visible everywhere it matters. Static array; no
allocator dependency.

    var vma_pool: [256]VMA
    var vma_free_head: int = 0
    var vma_pool_init = false

`vma_module_init` is idempotent and called lazily by `vma_alloc`.
The first allocation links every slot into the free list. Doing
it lazily keeps `kernel_init` free of an explicit init call.

    vma_module_init()
        if vma_pool_init
            return
        var i = 0
        while i < MAX_VMAS - 1
            vma_pool[i].next_free = i + 1
            i += 1
        vma_pool[MAX_VMAS - 1].next_free = VMA_NIL
        vma_free_head = 0
        vma_pool_init = true

Take a VMA from the free list and zero its tree-node fields. The
caller fills in start/end/prot/flags/fd/offset before inserting.

    vma_alloc() -> int
        vma_module_init()
        val idx = vma_free_head
        if idx == VMA_NIL
            return VMA_NIL
        vma_free_head = vma_pool[idx].next_free
        vma_pool[idx].left   = VMA_NIL
        vma_pool[idx].right  = VMA_NIL
        vma_pool[idx].parent = VMA_NIL
        vma_pool[idx].color  = VMA_RB_RED
        vma_pool[idx].next_free = VMA_NIL
        idx

Return a VMA to the free list. Caller is responsible for having
already removed it from any tree.

    vma_free(idx: int)
        if idx == VMA_NIL
            return
        vma_pool[idx].next_free = vma_free_head
        vma_free_head = idx

Initialize a freshly-allocated `VMATree` to "empty". Always called
from process creation.

    vma_tree_init(t: *VMATree)
        t.root = VMA_NIL

Color helpers — NIL is treated as BLACK.

    vma_color(idx: int) -> int
        if idx == VMA_NIL
            return VMA_RB_BLACK
        vma_pool[idx].color

    vma_set_color(idx: int, c: int)
        if idx != VMA_NIL
            vma_pool[idx].color = c

Standard BST rotations. `rotate_left` at `x` makes `x.right`
the new subtree root.

    vma_rotate_left(t: *VMATree, x: int)
        val y = vma_pool[x].right
        vma_pool[x].right = vma_pool[y].left
        if vma_pool[y].left != VMA_NIL
            vma_pool[vma_pool[y].left].parent = x
        vma_pool[y].parent = vma_pool[x].parent
        if vma_pool[x].parent == VMA_NIL
            t.root = y
        else
            if x == vma_pool[vma_pool[x].parent].left
                vma_pool[vma_pool[x].parent].left = y
            else
                vma_pool[vma_pool[x].parent].right = y
        vma_pool[y].left = x
        vma_pool[x].parent = y

    vma_rotate_right(t: *VMATree, y: int)
        val x = vma_pool[y].left
        vma_pool[y].left = vma_pool[x].right
        if vma_pool[x].right != VMA_NIL
            vma_pool[vma_pool[x].right].parent = y
        vma_pool[x].parent = vma_pool[y].parent
        if vma_pool[y].parent == VMA_NIL
            t.root = x
        else
            if y == vma_pool[vma_pool[y].parent].left
                vma_pool[vma_pool[y].parent].left = x
            else
                vma_pool[vma_pool[y].parent].right = x
        vma_pool[x].right = y
        vma_pool[y].parent = x

Restore red-black invariants after insertion. `z` is the freshly-
inserted (red) node. Walk up fixing red-red violations by
recoloring or rotating; the root is forced BLACK at the end.

    vma_insert_fixup(t: *VMATree, z_in: int)
        var z = z_in
        while vma_pool[z].parent != VMA_NIL
            val p = vma_pool[z].parent
            if vma_pool[p].color != VMA_RB_RED
                break
            val gp = vma_pool[p].parent
            if gp == VMA_NIL
                break
            if p == vma_pool[gp].left
                val uncle = vma_pool[gp].right
                if vma_color(uncle) == VMA_RB_RED
                    vma_pool[p].color = VMA_RB_BLACK
                    vma_set_color(uncle, VMA_RB_BLACK)
                    vma_pool[gp].color = VMA_RB_RED
                    z = gp
                else
                    if z == vma_pool[p].right
                        z = p
                        vma_rotate_left(t, z)
                    val p2 = vma_pool[z].parent
                    val gp2 = vma_pool[p2].parent
                    vma_pool[p2].color = VMA_RB_BLACK
                    vma_pool[gp2].color = VMA_RB_RED
                    vma_rotate_right(t, gp2)
            else
                val uncle = vma_pool[gp].left
                if vma_color(uncle) == VMA_RB_RED
                    vma_pool[p].color = VMA_RB_BLACK
                    vma_set_color(uncle, VMA_RB_BLACK)
                    vma_pool[gp].color = VMA_RB_RED
                    z = gp
                else
                    if z == vma_pool[p].left
                        z = p
                        vma_rotate_right(t, z)
                    val p2 = vma_pool[z].parent
                    val gp2 = vma_pool[p2].parent
                    vma_pool[p2].color = VMA_RB_BLACK
                    vma_pool[gp2].color = VMA_RB_RED
                    vma_rotate_left(t, gp2)
        vma_pool[t.root].color = VMA_RB_BLACK

Insert a fresh VMA into the tree, keyed on `start`. Caller has
already filled in start/end/prot/flags/fd/offset on the freshly
allocated index. Returns the inserted node index (same as `idx`)
for convenience. Does *not* check for overlap — callers are
expected to use `vma_lookup_addr` first when overlap matters.

    vma_insert(t: *VMATree, idx: int)
        var parent = VMA_NIL
        var cur = t.root
        val key = vma_pool[idx].vstart
        while cur != VMA_NIL
            parent = cur
            if key < vma_pool[cur].vstart
                cur = vma_pool[cur].left
            else
                cur = vma_pool[cur].right
        vma_pool[idx].parent = parent
        if parent == VMA_NIL
            t.root = idx
        else
            if key < vma_pool[parent].vstart
                vma_pool[parent].left = idx
            else
                vma_pool[parent].right = idx
        vma_insert_fixup(t, idx)

Convenience wrapper: allocate a VMA, fill it in, insert it,
return the index. Returns `VMA_NIL` if the pool is exhausted.

    vma_create(t: *VMATree, vstart: u64, vend: u64, prot: int, flags: int, fd: int, offset: u64) -> int
        val idx = vma_alloc()
        if idx == VMA_NIL
            return VMA_NIL
        vma_pool[idx].vstart  = vstart
        vma_pool[idx].vend    = vend
        vma_pool[idx].prot   = prot
        vma_pool[idx].flags  = flags
        vma_pool[idx].fd     = fd
        vma_pool[idx].offset = offset
        vma_insert(t, idx)
        idx

Point query: which VMA covers `addr`? Returns the VMA index, or
`VMA_NIL` if no VMA covers `addr`.

The query exploits the disjoint-VMA invariant: walk down the BST
tracking the largest node whose start ≤ addr; that is the only
candidate, and it covers `addr` iff `addr < end`.

    vma_lookup_addr(t: *VMATree, addr: u64) -> int
        var cur = t.root
        var best = VMA_NIL
        while cur != VMA_NIL
            if vma_pool[cur].vstart <= addr
                best = cur
                cur = vma_pool[cur].right
            else
                cur = vma_pool[cur].left
        if best == VMA_NIL
            return VMA_NIL
        if addr < vma_pool[best].vend
            return best
        VMA_NIL

In-order successor / predecessor — used by `vma_remove` and by
range walks (chunks 4-6). NIL if none.

    vma_min(idx_in: int) -> int
        if idx_in == VMA_NIL
            return VMA_NIL
        var cur = idx_in
        while vma_pool[cur].left != VMA_NIL
            cur = vma_pool[cur].left
        cur

    vma_first(t: *VMATree) -> int
        vma_min(t.root)

    vma_next(idx: int) -> int
        if idx == VMA_NIL
            return VMA_NIL
        if vma_pool[idx].right != VMA_NIL
            return vma_min(vma_pool[idx].right)
        var cur = idx
        var p = vma_pool[cur].parent
        while p != VMA_NIL
            if vma_pool[p].left == cur
                return p
            cur = p
            p = vma_pool[cur].parent
        VMA_NIL

Replace one subtree by another. `transplant(u, v)` swaps `v` into
`u`'s position in the tree; `u` becomes detached.

    vma_transplant(t: *VMATree, u: int, v: int)
        if vma_pool[u].parent == VMA_NIL
            t.root = v
        else
            val p = vma_pool[u].parent
            if u == vma_pool[p].left
                vma_pool[p].left = v
            else
                vma_pool[p].right = v
        if v != VMA_NIL
            vma_pool[v].parent = vma_pool[u].parent

Restore red-black invariants after removal. `x` is the node that
took the place of the removed black node (possibly NIL); `xp` is
its parent (tracked separately because `x` may be NIL and have no
parent pointer of its own).

    vma_remove_fixup(t: *VMATree, x_in: int, xp_in: int)
        var x = x_in
        var xp = xp_in
        while x != t.root
            if vma_color(x) == VMA_RB_RED
                break
            if xp == VMA_NIL
                break
            if x == vma_pool[xp].left
                var w = vma_pool[xp].right
                if w == VMA_NIL
                    break
                if vma_pool[w].color == VMA_RB_RED
                    vma_pool[w].color = VMA_RB_BLACK
                    vma_pool[xp].color = VMA_RB_RED
                    vma_rotate_left(t, xp)
                    w = vma_pool[xp].right
                    if w == VMA_NIL
                        break
                if vma_color(vma_pool[w].left) == VMA_RB_BLACK
                    if vma_color(vma_pool[w].right) == VMA_RB_BLACK
                        vma_pool[w].color = VMA_RB_RED
                        x = xp
                        xp = vma_pool[x].parent
                        continue
                if vma_color(vma_pool[w].right) == VMA_RB_BLACK
                    vma_set_color(vma_pool[w].left, VMA_RB_BLACK)
                    vma_pool[w].color = VMA_RB_RED
                    vma_rotate_right(t, w)
                    w = vma_pool[xp].right
                vma_pool[w].color = vma_pool[xp].color
                vma_pool[xp].color = VMA_RB_BLACK
                vma_set_color(vma_pool[w].right, VMA_RB_BLACK)
                vma_rotate_left(t, xp)
                x = t.root
                break
            else
                var w = vma_pool[xp].left
                if w == VMA_NIL
                    break
                if vma_pool[w].color == VMA_RB_RED
                    vma_pool[w].color = VMA_RB_BLACK
                    vma_pool[xp].color = VMA_RB_RED
                    vma_rotate_right(t, xp)
                    w = vma_pool[xp].left
                    if w == VMA_NIL
                        break
                if vma_color(vma_pool[w].right) == VMA_RB_BLACK
                    if vma_color(vma_pool[w].left) == VMA_RB_BLACK
                        vma_pool[w].color = VMA_RB_RED
                        x = xp
                        xp = vma_pool[x].parent
                        continue
                if vma_color(vma_pool[w].left) == VMA_RB_BLACK
                    vma_set_color(vma_pool[w].right, VMA_RB_BLACK)
                    vma_pool[w].color = VMA_RB_RED
                    vma_rotate_left(t, w)
                    w = vma_pool[xp].left
                vma_pool[w].color = vma_pool[xp].color
                vma_pool[xp].color = VMA_RB_BLACK
                vma_set_color(vma_pool[w].left, VMA_RB_BLACK)
                vma_rotate_right(t, xp)
                x = t.root
                break
        vma_set_color(x, VMA_RB_BLACK)

Detach a VMA from the tree and return its slot to the pool. The
node index is invalidated after this call.

    vma_remove(t: *VMATree, z: int)
        if z == VMA_NIL
            return
        val y_orig_color = vma_pool[z].color
        var x = VMA_NIL
        var xp = VMA_NIL
        if vma_pool[z].left == VMA_NIL
            x = vma_pool[z].right
            xp = vma_pool[z].parent
            vma_transplant(t, z, vma_pool[z].right)
        else
            if vma_pool[z].right == VMA_NIL
                x = vma_pool[z].left
                xp = vma_pool[z].parent
                vma_transplant(t, z, vma_pool[z].left)
            else
                var y = vma_pool[z].right
                while vma_pool[y].left != VMA_NIL
                    y = vma_pool[y].left
                val y_color = vma_pool[y].color
                x = vma_pool[y].right
                if vma_pool[y].parent == z
                    xp = y
                else
                    xp = vma_pool[y].parent
                    vma_transplant(t, y, vma_pool[y].right)
                    vma_pool[y].right = vma_pool[z].right
                    vma_pool[vma_pool[y].right].parent = y
                vma_transplant(t, z, y)
                vma_pool[y].left = vma_pool[z].left
                vma_pool[vma_pool[y].left].parent = y
                vma_pool[y].color = vma_pool[z].color
                if y_color == VMA_RB_BLACK
                    vma_remove_fixup(t, x, xp)
                vma_free(z)
                return
        if y_orig_color == VMA_RB_BLACK
            vma_remove_fixup(t, x, xp)
        vma_free(z)

Split a VMA at `addr` (which must satisfy `start < addr < end`).
The original VMA is shrunk to `[start, addr)`; a new VMA covering
`[addr, end)` with the same prot/flags/fd is allocated and
inserted. Returns the new (right-half) VMA's index, or VMA_NIL on
allocator failure or invalid `addr`.

For file-backed VMAs, the right half's `offset` advances by
`(addr - original_start)` so file-byte alignment is preserved.

    vma_split(t: *VMATree, idx: int, addr: u64) -> int
        if idx == VMA_NIL
            return VMA_NIL
        if addr <= vma_pool[idx].vstart
            return VMA_NIL
        if addr >= vma_pool[idx].vend
            return VMA_NIL
        val new_idx = vma_alloc()
        if new_idx == VMA_NIL
            return VMA_NIL
        val orig_start = vma_pool[idx].vstart
        val orig_end   = vma_pool[idx].vend
        vma_pool[new_idx].vstart  = addr
        vma_pool[new_idx].vend    = orig_end
        vma_pool[new_idx].prot   = vma_pool[idx].prot
        vma_pool[new_idx].flags  = vma_pool[idx].flags
        vma_pool[new_idx].fd     = vma_pool[idx].fd
        vma_pool[new_idx].offset = vma_pool[idx].offset + (addr - orig_start)
        vma_pool[idx].vend = addr
        vma_insert(t, new_idx)
        new_idx

Tear down every VMA in a process. Used by `reap_process` and by
the future `execve` path. After the call, the tree is empty and
every node is back on the free list.

We can't walk the tree while remove-rebalancing it, so we collect
indices into a small stack via repeated `vma_first` calls. Pool
size bounds the total work.

    vma_clear_all(t: *VMATree)
        var n = vma_first(t)
        while n != VMA_NIL
            vma_remove(t, n)
            n = vma_first(t)

Counts. Used by tests; cheap to compute via in-order walk.

    vma_count(t: *VMATree) -> int
        var c = 0
        var n = vma_first(t)
        while n != VMA_NIL
            c += 1
            n = vma_next(n)
        c

Page-fault entry point. The arch handlers (x86 page-fault ISR,
aarch64 EL0 sync) call this with the faulting `vaddr`, the
process's `pid` and `ptbr`, and a `write` flag (1 if the fault
was caused by a store, 0 if a load or instruction fetch).

Returns 0 if the fault was satisfied (a frame was installed and
the faulting instruction can retry), -1 if no VMA covers the
address or the fault couldn't be handled here. The arch code
falls through to its legacy "kill process" path on -1.

Two distinct dispositions, separated by whether the leaf PTE is
already present:

  - **PTE absent** — first touch of an anonymous page. Allocate a
    zero frame via `kalloc_user_page` (refcount=1) and install it.
    Read/exec/write all funnel through this path on first access.

  - **PTE present** (write fault only — RO reads don't trap on
    either arch) — copy-on-write. The frame is shared (refcount
    set by some prior path: chunk-6 fork, the chunk-5 selftest's
    `sys_cow_share_self`, or a future shared-anon mapping). We
    allocate a fresh frame, copy the old contents into it, install
    the new frame writable, then drop our reference to the old
    frame. If we held the last ref the old frame returns to the
    page pool; otherwise it stays mapped wherever else it lives.

Shared mappings (MAP_SHARED) write-faulting on a RO PTE would
propagate the change to all sharers; the chunk-5 path doesn't yet
implement that, so we decline. MAP_PRIVATE is the only flag that
exists in chunk-5 user-space anyway.

    vma_handle_fault(t: *VMATree, vaddr: u64, ptbr: u64, write: int) -> int
        val v = vma_lookup_addr(t, vaddr)
        if v == VMA_NIL
            return -1
        if (vma_pool[v].flags & VMA_MAP_ANON) == 0
            return -1
        if write != 0
            if (vma_pool[v].prot & VMA_PROT_WRITE) == 0
                return -1
        else
            if (vma_pool[v].prot & VMA_PROT_READ) == 0
                return -1

        val page_va = vaddr & ~u64(0xFFF)
        var writable = 0
        if (vma_pool[v].prot & VMA_PROT_WRITE) != 0
            writable = 1
        var executable = 0
        if (vma_pool[v].prot & VMA_PROT_EXEC) != 0
            executable = 1

        val existing_pa = vm_v2p(ptbr, page_va)
        if existing_pa != u64(0)
            // PTE present — only reachable through a write fault on a
            // RO PTE. Defensive: a read fault on a present page should
            // never trap, but if it does, decline rather than silently
            // re-zero the page.
            if write == 0
                return -1
            if (vma_pool[v].flags & VMA_MAP_PRIVATE) == 0
                return -1
            val new_pa = kalloc_user_page()
            if new_pa == u64(0)
                return -1
            // Copy old frame → new frame. Both PAs sit in the page
            // pool, which both arches identity-map in kernel context
            // (x86 boot.s pd[0..511] superpages, aarch64 L1[1] block),
            // so PA = VA when reading from kernel mode.
            var src: *byte = *byte(existing_pa)
            var dst: *byte = *byte(new_pa)
            var i = 0
            while i < PAGE_SIZE
                dst[i] = src[i]
                i += 1
            if vm_install_user_page(ptbr, page_va, new_pa, writable, executable) != 0
                kfree_user_page(new_pa)
                return -1
            kfree_user_page(existing_pa)
            return 0

PTE absent — first-touch anonymous demand-page. `kalloc_user_page`
returns a zeroed frame at refcount=1.

        val pa = kalloc_user_page()
        if pa == u64(0)
            return -1
        if vm_install_user_page(ptbr, page_va, pa, writable, executable) != 0
            kfree_user_page(pa)
            return -1
        0


Selftest -- exercises the public surface and validates invariants
without going through any kernel state. Used by the chunk-1
test program via a debug syscall.

Returns 0 on success; 1..N on failure at step N.

    vma_selftest() -> int
        var t: VMATree
        vma_tree_init(&t)

        // Step 1 — insert three disjoint VMAs in non-sorted order.
        val a = vma_create(&t, u64(0x10000), u64(0x20000), VMA_PROT_READ, VMA_MAP_ANON | VMA_MAP_PRIVATE, -1, u64(0))
        if a == VMA_NIL
            return 1
        val b = vma_create(&t, u64(0x40000), u64(0x50000), VMA_PROT_READ | VMA_PROT_WRITE, VMA_MAP_ANON | VMA_MAP_PRIVATE, -1, u64(0))
        if b == VMA_NIL
            return 1
        val c = vma_create(&t, u64(0x30000), u64(0x35000), VMA_PROT_READ, VMA_MAP_ANON | VMA_MAP_PRIVATE, -1, u64(0))
        if c == VMA_NIL
            return 1
        if vma_count(&t) != 3
            return 2

        // Step 3 — point lookups inside, at boundaries, between.
        if vma_lookup_addr(&t, u64(0x10000)) != a
            return 3
        if vma_lookup_addr(&t, u64(0x1FFFF)) != a
            return 3
        if vma_lookup_addr(&t, u64(0x20000)) != VMA_NIL
            return 3
        if vma_lookup_addr(&t, u64(0x32000)) != c
            return 3
        if vma_lookup_addr(&t, u64(0x45678)) != b
            return 3
        if vma_lookup_addr(&t, u64(0x60000)) != VMA_NIL
            return 3

        // Step 4 — split b at midpoint; verify both halves still resolve.
        val b_right = vma_split(&t, b, u64(0x48000))
        if b_right == VMA_NIL
            return 4
        if vma_count(&t) != 4
            return 4
        if vma_lookup_addr(&t, u64(0x47000)) != b
            return 4
        if vma_lookup_addr(&t, u64(0x49000)) != b_right
            return 4
        if vma_pool[b].vend != u64(0x48000)
            return 4
        if vma_pool[b_right].vstart != u64(0x48000)
            return 4
        if vma_pool[b_right].vend != u64(0x50000)
            return 4

        // Step 5 — bad split args reject without leaking a slot.
        val pre_count = vma_count(&t)
        if vma_split(&t, a, u64(0x10000)) != VMA_NIL
            return 5
        if vma_split(&t, a, u64(0x20000)) != VMA_NIL
            return 5
        if vma_split(&t, a, u64(0x80000)) != VMA_NIL
            return 5
        if vma_count(&t) != pre_count
            return 5

        // Step 6 — remove the right-half of b and verify the lookup
        // for that range now misses.
        vma_remove(&t, b_right)
        if vma_count(&t) != 3
            return 6
        if vma_lookup_addr(&t, u64(0x49000)) != VMA_NIL
            return 6
        if vma_lookup_addr(&t, u64(0x47000)) != b
            return 6

        // Step 7 — vma_first / vma_next yield VMAs in ascending order.
        var prev_start: u64 = 0
        var n = vma_first(&t)
        while n != VMA_NIL
            if vma_pool[n].vstart < prev_start
                return 7
            prev_start = vma_pool[n].vstart
            n = vma_next(n)

        // Step 8 — clear_all returns every slot to the pool.
        vma_clear_all(&t)
        if vma_count(&t) != 0
            return 8
        if t.root != VMA_NIL
            return 8

        // Step 9 — large fan-out exercise that forces rebalancing.
        // Insert 64 VMAs with strides of 2 pages, then pick three at
        // random and remove them, then walk in order and verify
        // count + monotonicity.
        var i = 0
        while i < 64
            val s = u64(0x100000) + u64(i) * u64(0x2000)
            val e = s + u64(0x1000)
            if vma_create(&t, s, e, VMA_PROT_READ, VMA_MAP_ANON | VMA_MAP_PRIVATE, -1, u64(0)) == VMA_NIL
                return 9
            i += 1
        if vma_count(&t) != 64
            return 9
        // Remove the 0th, 32nd, and 63rd by point-lookup.
        val r0 = vma_lookup_addr(&t, u64(0x100000))
        val r1 = vma_lookup_addr(&t, u64(0x100000) + u64(32) * u64(0x2000))
        val r2 = vma_lookup_addr(&t, u64(0x100000) + u64(63) * u64(0x2000))
        if r0 == VMA_NIL
            return 9
        if r1 == VMA_NIL
            return 9
        if r2 == VMA_NIL
            return 9
        vma_remove(&t, r0)
        vma_remove(&t, r1)
        vma_remove(&t, r2)
        if vma_count(&t) != 61
            return 9
        // Walk + monotonicity check.
        var prev: u64 = 0
        var n2 = vma_first(&t)
        while n2 != VMA_NIL
            if vma_pool[n2].vstart < prev
                return 9
            prev = vma_pool[n2].vstart
            n2 = vma_next(n2)
        vma_clear_all(&t)

        0
